WEBVTT

00:00:06.773 --> 00:00:08.638
Whatever she wants us for,
it better be good.

00:00:08.675 --> 00:00:09.642
Bridge.

00:00:09.676 --> 00:00:11.303
I had you right
where I wanted you.

00:00:11.344 --> 00:00:12.902
What are you talking about?

00:00:12.946 --> 00:00:15.779
I was ahead... 19-7.

00:00:15.815 --> 00:00:18.147
I was just lulling you
into a false sense of security.

00:00:18.184 --> 00:00:19.151
Sure you were.

00:00:19.185 --> 00:00:20.345
I'll win the next
couple of points,

00:00:20.387 --> 00:00:21.911
then you'll start to tense up.

00:00:21.955 --> 00:00:25.186
I do not tense up.

00:00:25.225 --> 00:00:26.954
Easy, B'Elanna.

00:00:26.993 --> 00:00:28.358
It's only hoverball.

00:00:28.395 --> 00:00:29.657
You wanted to see us, Captain?

00:00:29.696 --> 00:00:30.663
Yes, Commander.

00:00:30.697 --> 00:00:32.631
We've picked up
an intriguing transmission.

00:00:32.665 --> 00:00:33.689
I have a source on the signal.

00:00:33.733 --> 00:00:34.700
A ship?

00:00:34.734 --> 00:00:35.701
Negative.

00:00:35.735 --> 00:00:37.066
It appears to be
a beacon of some kind.

00:00:37.103 --> 00:00:38.502
A beacon?

00:00:40.006 --> 00:00:40.973
We are being hailed

00:00:41.007 --> 00:00:42.872
by someone using
a Federation signal.

00:02:33.384 --> 00:02:34.646
How could someone
be transmitting

00:02:34.686 --> 00:02:36.984
a Federation signal
from the Delta Quadrant?

00:02:37.021 --> 00:02:39.854
Maybe Starfleet found a way
to get a probe here.

00:02:39.891 --> 00:02:41.449
Maybe they're looking for us.

00:02:41.492 --> 00:02:43.187
I'd like to believe that, too,

00:02:43.228 --> 00:02:45.162
but let's not jump
to conclusions.

00:02:45.196 --> 00:02:46.720
See if you can
authenticate the signal.

00:02:46.764 --> 00:02:48.026
The carrier wave frequency

00:02:48.066 --> 00:02:50.694
does correspond to standard
Starfleet security codes.

00:02:50.735 --> 00:02:51.702
As of when?

00:02:51.736 --> 00:02:52.998
According to the encryption key,

00:02:53.037 --> 00:02:54.595
this particular code
was not scheduled

00:02:54.639 --> 00:02:57.506
for implementation
until Stardate 48423.

00:02:57.609 --> 00:02:59.907
That's a month after we left
Deep Space 9.

00:02:59.944 --> 00:03:02.412
They must be looking for us.

00:03:02.447 --> 00:03:04.278
Your optimism may be
premature, Mr. Kim.

00:03:04.315 --> 00:03:05.782
Sorry, Captain.

00:03:05.817 --> 00:03:07.182
But it's also infectious.

00:03:07.218 --> 00:03:10.847
Mr. Paris,
lay in a course for the beacon.

00:03:10.889 --> 00:03:12.288
Yes, ma'am.

00:03:19.597 --> 00:03:22.327
We're approaching the beacon's
coordinates, Captain.

00:03:22.367 --> 00:03:25.632
It's drifted inside
an ionized hydrogen cloud.

00:03:25.670 --> 00:03:27.467
The cloud's interfering
with our sensor readings.

00:03:27.505 --> 00:03:29.735
Can you get any information
from the beacon?

00:03:29.774 --> 00:03:30.866
I'm afraid not.

00:03:30.909 --> 00:03:31.898
Should I beam it aboard?

00:03:31.943 --> 00:03:33.570
I'd advise against bringing it

00:03:33.611 --> 00:03:35.272
on board before we've
gotten a look at it...

00:03:35.313 --> 00:03:37.008
even if it is emitting
a Federation signal.

00:03:37.048 --> 00:03:39.278
Agreed, and I don't want
to fly blindly

00:03:39.317 --> 00:03:40.841
into a hydrogen cloud either.

00:03:40.885 --> 00:03:43.080
Mr. Tuvok, tractor the probe
into sensor range.

00:03:43.121 --> 00:03:44.088
Aye, Captain.

00:03:44.122 --> 00:03:45.248
Targeting scanners locked.

00:03:45.290 --> 00:03:46.279
Initiating tractor beam.

00:03:47.292 --> 00:03:48.350
Report.

00:03:48.393 --> 00:03:50.361
We are taking fire
from inside the cloud.

00:03:50.395 --> 00:03:51.362
Source?

00:03:51.396 --> 00:03:52.363
Unknown.

00:03:52.397 --> 00:03:53.421
Battle stations.

00:04:03.308 --> 00:04:06.106
A Kazon raider is closing
at 158 mark 9.

00:04:06.144 --> 00:04:07.702
Hail them, Mr. Kim.

00:04:08.813 --> 00:04:10.178
They're not responding, Captain.

00:04:10.214 --> 00:04:12.444
Warp 3, Mr. Paris.
Get us out of here.

00:04:12.517 --> 00:04:13.506
Aye...

00:04:14.986 --> 00:04:16.954
Warp engines are off-line,
Captain.

00:04:16.988 --> 00:04:18.853
Initiate evasive pattern
omega three.

00:04:18.890 --> 00:04:20.585
Mr. Tuvok, return fire.

00:04:20.625 --> 00:04:21.990
Aye, Captain.

00:04:23.594 --> 00:04:25.323
Kazon ship is in pursuit.

00:04:25.363 --> 00:04:28.230
An opening is forming
in the starboard shields,

00:04:28.266 --> 00:04:29.460
72 centimeters in diameter.

00:04:29.534 --> 00:04:31.331
See if you can close it,
Commander.

00:04:31.369 --> 00:04:32.927
Try rotating
the shield harmonics.

00:04:35.640 --> 00:04:36.937
They are continuously

00:04:36.975 --> 00:04:39.603
matching their weapons frequency
to our shield frequency.

00:04:39.644 --> 00:04:41.635
How the hell can they do that?

00:04:41.679 --> 00:04:42.976
I don't know.

00:04:43.014 --> 00:04:44.311
The diameter of the opening
has widened

00:04:44.349 --> 00:04:45.373
to approximately two meters.

00:04:45.416 --> 00:04:47.475
Set the shield harmonics
to rotate continuously.

00:04:47.552 --> 00:04:48.883
Aye, Commander.

00:04:48.920 --> 00:04:50.911
The diameter

00:04:50.955 --> 00:04:52.923
of the opening is now
approximately four meters.

00:04:52.957 --> 00:04:54.652
It's as if they know
our access codes.

00:04:54.692 --> 00:04:57.058
Captain, I am picking up
a smaller vessel

00:04:57.095 --> 00:04:58.494
emerging
from the hydrogen cloud.

00:04:58.596 --> 00:04:59.620
It is heading directly

00:04:59.664 --> 00:05:01.063
toward the opening
in our shields.

00:05:01.099 --> 00:05:03.397
All hands, brace for impact.

00:05:22.186 --> 00:05:26.247
Warning. Hull breach
on Deck 4, Cargo Bay 2.

00:05:26.290 --> 00:05:29.748
Structural integrity is
at 50 percent and dropping.

00:05:29.794 --> 00:05:32.126
The hull is starting to buckle.

00:05:32.163 --> 00:05:34.188
We're losing life support
on Deck 4.

00:05:34.232 --> 00:05:37.258
I am trying to initiate
an emergency containment field.

00:05:37.301 --> 00:05:38.461
However, the collision

00:05:38.536 --> 00:05:40.561
has caused a power failure
on Deck 4.

00:05:40.605 --> 00:05:42.869
Rerouting power to compensate.

00:05:44.409 --> 00:05:45.740
Containment field activated.

00:05:45.777 --> 00:05:49.213
Warning. Intruder alert
in Cargo Bay 2.

00:05:49.247 --> 00:05:50.942
Mr. Tuvok!

00:05:50.982 --> 00:05:52.313
Tuvok to Security.

00:05:52.350 --> 00:05:53.942
Meet me outside Cargo Bay 2.

00:05:53.985 --> 00:05:54.974
Aye, sir.

00:06:00.958 --> 00:06:02.687
Drop your weapons!

00:06:14.739 --> 00:06:15.706
It's no use.

00:06:15.740 --> 00:06:17.264
We're not going anywhere
with that shuttle

00:06:17.308 --> 00:06:18.275
sticking out of our side.

00:06:18.309 --> 00:06:19.776
It's totally destabilizing
our warp field.

00:06:19.811 --> 00:06:20.937
Mr. Kim,

00:06:20.978 --> 00:06:23.446
did you reroute power
to Transporter Room 2?

00:06:23.548 --> 00:06:24.708
No, sir.

00:06:24.749 --> 00:06:26.614
Bridge to Tuvok.

00:06:26.651 --> 00:06:27.879
Tuvok here.

00:06:27.919 --> 00:06:30.251
There may be intruders
in Transporter Room 2.

00:06:30.288 --> 00:06:31.277
I'm on my way.

00:06:49.207 --> 00:06:50.697
Tuvok to Bridge.

00:06:50.741 --> 00:06:51.708
Go ahead.

00:06:51.742 --> 00:06:53.073
The Kazon have beamed away,
Captain,

00:06:53.111 --> 00:06:55.136
and they've taken one of our
transporter modules with them.

00:06:55.179 --> 00:06:56.237
Can you lock on

00:06:56.280 --> 00:06:57.872
to the module and beam it back?

00:06:57.915 --> 00:06:58.904
Not at the moment.

00:06:58.950 --> 00:07:00.474
As soon as the Kazon
dematerialized,

00:07:00.518 --> 00:07:02.179
we lost all transporter power.

00:07:02.220 --> 00:07:05.053
Mr. Chakotay, lock a tractor
beam on to their ship.

00:07:05.089 --> 00:07:06.613
They're not leaving
with that module.

00:07:06.657 --> 00:07:08.249
Aye, Captain.

00:07:08.292 --> 00:07:10.317
The Kazon are powering
their warp engines, Captain.

00:07:10.361 --> 00:07:11.328
Make it fast, Commander.

00:07:11.362 --> 00:07:12.920
Engaging tractor beam.

00:07:12.964 --> 00:07:14.659
I've got them, Captain.

00:07:14.699 --> 00:07:17.099
The Kazon ship is hailing us.

00:07:17.135 --> 00:07:18.966
Suddenly they want to talk.

00:07:19.003 --> 00:07:20.197
On screen.

00:07:20.638 --> 00:07:23.607
Captain Janeway.

00:07:23.641 --> 00:07:26.542
First Maje Culluh
of the Kazon-Nistrim.

00:07:26.577 --> 00:07:28.807
I remember you, Culluh.

00:07:28.846 --> 00:07:31.246
That transporter module
you just stole

00:07:31.282 --> 00:07:33.409
is specifically designed
for our ship.

00:07:33.451 --> 00:07:35.112
You'll never be able
to integrate it

00:07:35.153 --> 00:07:36.450
into your systems.

00:07:36.521 --> 00:07:38.716
I've had some help
updating our technology

00:07:38.756 --> 00:07:40.690
since we last met.

00:07:48.032 --> 00:07:48.999
Seska?

00:07:49.033 --> 00:07:50.398
That's right, Captain.

00:07:50.434 --> 00:07:52.095
As you can see,
I'm in the process

00:07:52.136 --> 00:07:54.900
of restoring
my Cardassian physiology.

00:07:57.008 --> 00:07:59.135
Hello, Chakotay.

00:07:59.177 --> 00:08:01.543
I should have known
you were involved.

00:08:01.579 --> 00:08:03.945
Yes, you should have.

00:08:03.981 --> 00:08:07.178
Just like I knew you'd try
to stop us with a tractor beam.

00:08:07.218 --> 00:08:10.153
You've always been
so predictable.

00:08:11.622 --> 00:08:15.285
Captain, their deflector shields
are creating a feedback loop.

00:08:15.326 --> 00:08:17.157
It's neutralizing
the tractor emitter.

00:08:17.195 --> 00:08:19.060
Attempting to compensate.

00:08:19.096 --> 00:08:21.030
Good-bye, Chakotay.

00:08:21.065 --> 00:08:23.693
Lovely to see you again.

00:08:24.468 --> 00:08:26.595
It's too late.

00:08:26.637 --> 00:08:28.127
They've gone to warp.

00:08:35.680 --> 00:08:38.308
They modified the bow
to puncture our hull.

00:08:38.349 --> 00:08:42.115
I've never seen the Kazon
do anything like this before.

00:08:42.153 --> 00:08:45.350
Until now, the Kazon
have never had an advisor

00:08:45.389 --> 00:08:48.051
with Cardassian, Maquis
and Starfleet

00:08:48.092 --> 00:08:49.081
tactical experience.

00:08:49.126 --> 00:08:50.650
The question is:
How do we dislodge it

00:08:50.695 --> 00:08:52.162
without losing
structural integrity?

00:08:52.196 --> 00:08:53.891
With power down,
our containment field's

00:08:53.931 --> 00:08:55.330
already extremely unstable.

00:08:55.366 --> 00:08:57.095
We'll have to reroute
additional power

00:08:57.134 --> 00:08:58.294
to the containment field

00:08:58.336 --> 00:08:59.997
and tow their shuttle out
with one of our own.

00:09:00.037 --> 00:09:01.595
Then we can repair the breach.

00:09:01.639 --> 00:09:04.073
The shields and the warp drive
will have to wait.

00:09:04.108 --> 00:09:05.666
Warp drive isn't going
to do us much good

00:09:05.710 --> 00:09:07.371
with this knife
stuck in our belly.

00:09:07.411 --> 00:09:08.400
Get it out fast.

00:09:08.479 --> 00:09:09.411
We don't want the Kazon

00:09:09.480 --> 00:09:11.175
to put too much
distance between us.

00:09:11.215 --> 00:09:12.807
Forgive me, Captain,

00:09:12.850 --> 00:09:14.875
but are you sure
going after the Nistrim

00:09:14.919 --> 00:09:16.546
is the wisest course of action?

00:09:16.587 --> 00:09:18.646
After what they've
already done to us?

00:09:18.689 --> 00:09:20.748
Let me make something
very clear.

00:09:20.791 --> 00:09:24.124
The Nistrim are in possession
of Federation technology.

00:09:24.161 --> 00:09:26.129
That is
an unacceptable situation.

00:09:26.163 --> 00:09:30.429
Even though all they've stolen
is a small computer component?

00:09:30.468 --> 00:09:31.992
That "small component"
has the potential

00:09:32.036 --> 00:09:34.436
to cause vast problems
in this Quadrant.

00:09:34.505 --> 00:09:37.440
You're our resident
expert on the Kazon.

00:09:37.541 --> 00:09:39.634
What do you think the
other sects will do

00:09:39.677 --> 00:09:42.544
when they realize the Nistrim
have transporter capabilities?

00:09:42.580 --> 00:09:44.673
They'll try to get it for
themselves any way they can.

00:09:44.715 --> 00:09:45.807
You're right.

00:09:45.850 --> 00:09:48.216
It could alter the balance
of power among the sects.

00:09:48.252 --> 00:09:50.277
Exactly, and it is our duty

00:09:50.321 --> 00:09:52.255
to do everything we can,
no matter how dangerous

00:09:52.290 --> 00:09:53.848
to stop that from happening.

00:09:53.891 --> 00:09:55.449
You can count on me, Captain.

00:09:55.526 --> 00:09:57.619
From the look
of these sensor readings,

00:09:57.662 --> 00:09:59.687
Seska wants us
to come after her.

00:09:59.730 --> 00:10:01.197
Commander?

00:10:01.232 --> 00:10:04.133
I think Seska's leading us
into another trap.

00:10:04.168 --> 00:10:05.465
She masterminded

00:10:05.536 --> 00:10:06.901
a precision raid
that made us look

00:10:06.937 --> 00:10:08.302
like first-year
Academy students,

00:10:08.339 --> 00:10:10.807
but she left a warp trail
for us to follow.

00:10:10.841 --> 00:10:12.832
After such
a flawless performance,

00:10:12.877 --> 00:10:14.469
why would she suddenly make

00:10:14.545 --> 00:10:15.842
that kind of mistake?

00:10:15.880 --> 00:10:17.643
You think she wants more
than the transporter?

00:10:18.783 --> 00:10:20.717
Are you suggesting
we don't follow her?

00:10:20.751 --> 00:10:22.184
No, I agree
with everything you said

00:10:22.219 --> 00:10:24.380
about preventing
the spread of our technology,

00:10:24.422 --> 00:10:27.357
but conventional tactics
aren't going to work with Seska.

00:10:27.391 --> 00:10:29.450
We'll need to come at her
with a few surprises of our own.

00:10:29.493 --> 00:10:31.654
I'm open to suggestions.

00:10:31.696 --> 00:10:33.357
Perhaps Commander Chakotay

00:10:33.397 --> 00:10:35.490
could use
his intimate knowledge of Seska

00:10:35.533 --> 00:10:36.659
to manipulate her

00:10:36.701 --> 00:10:38.794
in much the same way
she manipulated us.

00:10:43.905 --> 00:10:45.429
It can move people
great distances

00:10:45.473 --> 00:10:47.600
in the blink of an eye, Haron,

00:10:47.642 --> 00:10:52.409
but this "transporter"
is only the beginning.

00:10:52.447 --> 00:10:53.914
Go on.

00:10:53.948 --> 00:10:55.006
I'm listening.

00:10:55.049 --> 00:10:58.212
There is a ship filled
with new technology.

00:10:58.253 --> 00:11:01.188
Devices that can make food,
water...

00:11:01.222 --> 00:11:04.020
even weapons...
appear out of thin air.

00:11:04.058 --> 00:11:07.926
A computer system which uses
neural tissue that can react

00:11:07.962 --> 00:11:09.862
twice as fast ours.

00:11:09.898 --> 00:11:12.059
Very interesting, Culluh,

00:11:12.100 --> 00:11:14.830
but what does all this
have to do with me?

00:11:16.004 --> 00:11:19.269
That ship is on its way here.

00:11:20.475 --> 00:11:24.502
Help us,
and we can divide the spoils.

00:11:32.086 --> 00:11:33.053
The module Seska stole

00:11:33.087 --> 00:11:35.351
contains a quantum
resonance oscillator.

00:11:35.390 --> 00:11:39.087
So, we modify this coil scanner
to detect the oscillator.

00:11:39.127 --> 00:11:40.992
Then we get close enough
to beam it back.

00:11:41.029 --> 00:11:42.360
I'm betting Seska's
figured out a way

00:11:42.397 --> 00:11:44.627
to shield the module
from our transporters.

00:11:44.666 --> 00:11:47.032
We might have
to destroy it instead.

00:11:47.068 --> 00:11:48.365
How do we do that?

00:11:48.403 --> 00:11:51.099
We borrow a trick
from Seska's book.

00:11:51.139 --> 00:11:52.902
Remember how we disabled
the computer core

00:11:52.941 --> 00:11:55.273
on the Cardassian frigate
orbiting Bajor?

00:11:55.310 --> 00:11:58.370
Seska modified
an antiproton beam

00:11:58.413 --> 00:12:00.142
to penetrate
its shields and hull.

00:12:00.181 --> 00:12:01.205
Exactly.

00:12:01.249 --> 00:12:02.682
But if I remember correctly,

00:12:02.717 --> 00:12:05.982
the beam was only effective
from an extremely close range.

00:12:06.020 --> 00:12:07.954
How do we get near enough
to the Nistrim ship?

00:12:07.989 --> 00:12:09.923
One thing at a time.

00:12:11.693 --> 00:12:13.820
You're taking this all very
personally, aren't you?

00:12:13.862 --> 00:12:15.193
Why shouldn't I?

00:12:15.230 --> 00:12:18.358
You are not responsible
for what happened.

00:12:18.399 --> 00:12:21.732
Oh, no?
I let her join the Maquis.

00:12:21.769 --> 00:12:23.464
I took her into my confidence.

00:12:23.504 --> 00:12:25.972
I even got...

00:12:26.007 --> 00:12:28.032
intimately involved with her.

00:12:28.076 --> 00:12:30.840
So you have
lousy taste in women.

00:12:30.879 --> 00:12:34.838
Look, Chakotay,
she fooled us all.

00:12:34.883 --> 00:12:37.579
She was my best friend...

00:12:37.619 --> 00:12:39.849
or at least
that's what I thought.

00:12:39.888 --> 00:12:43.119
Well, I, for one, am through
being manipulated by her.

00:12:43.157 --> 00:12:44.920
Are you sure?

00:12:44.959 --> 00:12:47.325
Because she's affecting you.

00:12:47.362 --> 00:12:50.263
That's just where she wants you.

00:12:50.298 --> 00:12:53.131
Don't tense up.

00:12:56.237 --> 00:12:57.499
So now I'm getting advice

00:12:57.538 --> 00:12:59.972
about controlling
my emotions from you.

00:13:03.778 --> 00:13:07.942
Our sects have been
blood enemies for generations.

00:13:07.982 --> 00:13:12.112
And yet, now you ask for my help
to defeat this Voyager.

00:13:12.153 --> 00:13:14.587
Why not simply do it yourselves?

00:13:14.622 --> 00:13:16.180
I'll tell you why.

00:13:16.224 --> 00:13:18.749
Because the Nistrim are weak

00:13:18.793 --> 00:13:21.728
and the Relora are strong.

00:13:21.763 --> 00:13:26.097
Your grandfather's time
has passed, Culluh.

00:13:26.134 --> 00:13:30.195
You've presided over the demise
of your own sect, whittled away

00:13:30.238 --> 00:13:32.001
- your strength...
- Enough!

00:13:35.643 --> 00:13:39.602
You may have ships
and soldiers,

00:13:39.647 --> 00:13:43.242
but I have the technology.

00:13:45.586 --> 00:13:47.144
And I congratulate you

00:13:47.188 --> 00:13:49.986
on the daring and cunning
of your raid.

00:13:50.024 --> 00:13:55.018
Now, why don't you give me
this transporter technology...

00:13:55.063 --> 00:13:56.792
assuming it's authentic...

00:13:56.831 --> 00:14:00.130
and let the Relora do
what we do best.

00:14:00.168 --> 00:14:02.136
When we have defeated
the Voyager,

00:14:02.170 --> 00:14:05.196
we will not forget
the Nistrim's assistance.

00:14:05.239 --> 00:14:08.037
You think I'm a fool.

00:14:08.076 --> 00:14:14.811
I won't hand this
technology over to you.

00:14:14.849 --> 00:14:17.784
Then perhaps we
will have to take it.

00:14:19.754 --> 00:14:23.121
Why don't we let the maje
go back to his ship

00:14:23.157 --> 00:14:25.091
while we consider his offer?

00:14:25.126 --> 00:14:28.061
Listen to your woman,
Culluh.

00:14:39.741 --> 00:14:40.799
I'm picking up a gap

00:14:40.842 --> 00:14:42.810
in the Nistrim's warp trail,
Captain.

00:14:42.844 --> 00:14:44.971
All stop.
Let's take a look.

00:14:45.013 --> 00:14:46.947
Captain, I've got
some floating debris

00:14:46.981 --> 00:14:48.949
at bearing 319 mark 4.

00:14:48.983 --> 00:14:50.450
On screen.

00:14:51.819 --> 00:14:53.252
What is it?

00:14:53.287 --> 00:14:54.914
I'm not sure yet.

00:14:54.956 --> 00:14:56.116
Magnify.

00:15:06.534 --> 00:15:09.560
I'm detecting a residual
transporter signature.

00:15:09.604 --> 00:15:12.664
There is no doubt that this man
and his unfortunate companion

00:15:12.707 --> 00:15:13.799
were beamed into space.

00:15:13.841 --> 00:15:15.809
And according
to these readings,

00:15:15.843 --> 00:15:17.606
they were alive
at the time, Captain.

00:15:17.645 --> 00:15:20.079
It looks like Seska's
already adapted

00:15:20.114 --> 00:15:22.582
the transporter module
into the Kazon systems

00:15:22.617 --> 00:15:24.448
and started
experimenting with it.

00:15:24.485 --> 00:15:25.679
Her early trials

00:15:25.720 --> 00:15:28.712
appear to have been
less than successful.

00:15:28.756 --> 00:15:32.783
I'm not so sure these men died
by accident, Captain.

00:15:32.827 --> 00:15:35.227
You see this green band
he's wearing?

00:15:35.263 --> 00:15:39.461
It means he was the First Maje
of the Kazon-Relora.

00:15:39.534 --> 00:15:40.865
Relora?

00:15:40.902 --> 00:15:42.961
Sworn enemies of the Nistrim.

00:15:44.338 --> 00:15:47.569
It's conceivable
that Seska and Culluh

00:15:47.608 --> 00:15:51.271
used the transporter
to execute these men.

00:15:55.650 --> 00:15:59.916
Captain's Log, Stardate 49208.5.

00:15:59.954 --> 00:16:02.184
I have convened a meeting
of the senior staff

00:16:02.223 --> 00:16:04.555
to determine how we can get
close enough

00:16:04.592 --> 00:16:07.618
to the Nistrim ship
to deploy the antiproton beam.

00:16:09.931 --> 00:16:11.330
Where's Chakotay?

00:16:11.365 --> 00:16:12.332
He was in Engineering

00:16:12.366 --> 00:16:13.731
helping me modify
the coil scanner.

00:16:13.768 --> 00:16:15.030
He said he'd be right up.

00:16:15.069 --> 00:16:16.229
Janeway to Chakotay.

00:16:17.738 --> 00:16:19.433
Computer, locate
Commander Chakotay.

00:16:19.540 --> 00:16:22.202
Commander Chakotay
is not aboard the ship.

00:16:31.986 --> 00:16:34.420
Computer, when will we intercept
the Kazon vessel?

00:16:34.455 --> 00:16:36.423
Approximately 30 minutes.

00:16:40.962 --> 00:16:42.395
What I want to know, Mr. Tuvok,

00:16:42.430 --> 00:16:44.261
is how he was able to get
a shuttlecraft off this ship

00:16:44.298 --> 00:16:46.129
without either of us
knowing about it.

00:16:46.167 --> 00:16:49.034
Apparently, he was able to
override the lock-out command.

00:16:49.070 --> 00:16:50.401
I guess Seska's not the only one

00:16:50.438 --> 00:16:52.838
who knows how to compromise
our security systems.

00:16:52.874 --> 00:16:55.138
I assure you, Captain,
it will not happen again.

00:16:55.176 --> 00:16:56.473
See that it doesn't.

00:16:56.577 --> 00:16:59.011
Did Chakotay leave any clue
about what he's up to?

00:16:59.046 --> 00:17:01.037
I have accessed
his personal logs,

00:17:01.082 --> 00:17:02.709
but there is no reference
to his leaving Voyager.

00:17:02.750 --> 00:17:05.150
I guess he was in too big
a hurry to leave a note.

00:17:05.186 --> 00:17:06.517
The coil scanner was right here.

00:17:06.554 --> 00:17:07.612
He must have taken it with him.

00:17:08.823 --> 00:17:11.291
Then I guess it's pretty
clear he's going after Seska.

00:17:11.325 --> 00:17:12.292
Looks like that.

00:17:12.326 --> 00:17:13.725
You were working
with him, Lieutenant.

00:17:13.761 --> 00:17:15.023
Did he say anything to you?

00:17:15.062 --> 00:17:17.053
Just that he felt responsible

00:17:17.098 --> 00:17:18.998
for Seska,
and was determined to stop her,

00:17:19.033 --> 00:17:21.763
but I never thought he
would try to do this alone.

00:17:21.802 --> 00:17:23.292
How big a head start
does he have?

00:17:23.337 --> 00:17:24.895
Approximately three hours.

00:17:24.939 --> 00:17:26.099
Janeway to Conn.

00:17:26.140 --> 00:17:27.164
Paris here, Captain.

00:17:27.208 --> 00:17:28.334
Lay in a pursuit course

00:17:28.376 --> 00:17:30.435
for Commander Chakotay's
shuttlecraft, maximum impulse.

00:17:30.478 --> 00:17:31.445
Acknowledged.

00:17:31.479 --> 00:17:33.572
And Mr. Tuvok,
I want a complete review

00:17:33.614 --> 00:17:36.447
of all security protocols
on this ship by 2200 hours.

00:17:36.484 --> 00:17:38.782
Aye, Captain.

00:17:42.956 --> 00:17:44.753
You said the Relora
would join us.

00:17:44.791 --> 00:17:46.656
I should never
have listened to you.

00:17:46.693 --> 00:17:49.787
I was wrong.
I'm sorry.

00:17:49.830 --> 00:17:52.560
Kazon sects do not
help one another.

00:17:52.599 --> 00:17:54.965
Don't be so sure about that.

00:17:55.001 --> 00:17:56.628
What did you do

00:17:56.670 --> 00:17:58.160
to the two men
who refused your offer?

00:17:58.205 --> 00:17:59.172
I killed them.

00:17:59.206 --> 00:18:02.403
Yes, and by doing that,
you sent a message.

00:18:02.509 --> 00:18:04.977
"The Kazon-Nistrim
are powerful again.

00:18:05.011 --> 00:18:07.502
"First Maje Jal Culluh
has technology

00:18:07.547 --> 00:18:09.640
"that no other sect possesses.

00:18:09.683 --> 00:18:13.414
Join with him
or suffer the consequences."

00:18:13.486 --> 00:18:16.421
Maybe the mistake was
to approach the Relora.

00:18:16.523 --> 00:18:18.115
They're already strong.

00:18:18.158 --> 00:18:21.150
But the transporter
may be enough

00:18:21.194 --> 00:18:23.822
to convince
the Hobii to join me,

00:18:23.864 --> 00:18:25.388
and perhaps the Mostral.

00:18:25.432 --> 00:18:26.797
Yes,

00:18:26.833 --> 00:18:29.165
and with a few more ships,
you can defeat Voyager.

00:18:29.202 --> 00:18:31.602
And when you have
the rest of their technology,

00:18:31.638 --> 00:18:33.105
the other sects
will have no choice

00:18:33.139 --> 00:18:34.936
but to fall into line.

00:18:34.975 --> 00:18:37.443
That's why I sent
a subspace message

00:18:37.477 --> 00:18:41.038
to the Mostral
the Hobii and the Oglamar.

00:18:41.081 --> 00:18:42.207
You did what?

00:18:42.249 --> 00:18:44.979
I told them
about the transporter.

00:18:45.018 --> 00:18:46.508
Asked them to help us
take Voyager.

00:18:47.721 --> 00:18:49.814
You have gone too far.

00:18:49.856 --> 00:18:52.188
I sent the messages
in your name.

00:18:52.225 --> 00:18:54.284
I am the leader of this sect.

00:18:54.327 --> 00:18:57.057
You are only a woman.

00:18:57.097 --> 00:18:58.587
I'm sorry, Culluh.

00:18:58.632 --> 00:19:01.157
You will address me as Maje!

00:19:01.201 --> 00:19:03.669
Yes... Maje.

00:19:04.871 --> 00:19:07.635
Please...

00:19:07.674 --> 00:19:08.800
forgive me.

00:19:11.311 --> 00:19:13.609
So...

00:19:13.647 --> 00:19:19.176
how did the other sects
respond to my request?

00:19:19.219 --> 00:19:21.653
They're on their way to join us.

00:19:23.690 --> 00:19:26.284
I could do what no one has done

00:19:26.326 --> 00:19:29.022
since Jal Sankur
united the sects

00:19:29.062 --> 00:19:30.393
to overthrow the Trabe.

00:19:30.430 --> 00:19:31.419
Yes, Maje.

00:19:31.531 --> 00:19:33.829
I could have hundreds of ships

00:19:33.867 --> 00:19:36.392
and thousands of soldiers
under my command.

00:19:36.436 --> 00:19:38.199
Yes, Maje.

00:19:38.238 --> 00:19:42.174
I could be the most
powerful Kazon in the Quadrant.

00:19:42.208 --> 00:19:44.642
Yes, Maje.

00:19:56.890 --> 00:19:58.619
Come in.

00:19:58.658 --> 00:20:00.888
Do you have a minute, Captain?

00:20:00.927 --> 00:20:02.053
It's about Chakotay.

00:20:02.095 --> 00:20:03.460
That's not exactly
my favorite subject

00:20:03.496 --> 00:20:04.463
right now, Lieutenant.

00:20:04.497 --> 00:20:06.260
Well, I thought that
maybe I could explain...

00:20:06.299 --> 00:20:08.096
Explain what?
Why my First Officer

00:20:08.134 --> 00:20:09.396
publicly defied my authority

00:20:09.436 --> 00:20:11.461
by commandeering a shuttle
without permission?

00:20:11.571 --> 00:20:13.869
I know it was never
his intention to defy you.

00:20:13.907 --> 00:20:15.306
He respects your authority.

00:20:15.342 --> 00:20:16.366
But?

00:20:16.409 --> 00:20:17.967
But he's a very proud man,

00:20:18.011 --> 00:20:19.979
and he's been...

00:20:20.013 --> 00:20:22.481
embarrassed by Seska.

00:20:22.582 --> 00:20:24.777
What Seska did,
she did to all of us.

00:20:24.818 --> 00:20:26.445
Frankly, I find it

00:20:26.486 --> 00:20:28.647
more than a little
self-indulgent of Chakotay

00:20:28.688 --> 00:20:30.485
to assume this is all about him.

00:20:32.525 --> 00:20:35.494
He never said it
to me directly, but...

00:20:38.665 --> 00:20:40.656
I think he was
in love with her,

00:20:40.700 --> 00:20:42.895
and then he found out
that everything he knew

00:20:42.936 --> 00:20:44.870
about her was a lie.

00:20:44.904 --> 00:20:48.965
You said that he publicly
defied your authority.

00:20:49.009 --> 00:20:50.806
Can you imagine what
it must have been like

00:20:50.844 --> 00:20:52.607
for someone
as private as Chakotay

00:20:52.645 --> 00:20:56.809
to be publicly humiliated
by someone he loved?

00:20:56.850 --> 00:20:58.647
And then, as if
that weren't enough,

00:20:58.685 --> 00:20:59.845
she came back to taunt him

00:20:59.886 --> 00:21:01.444
in front
of the entire Bridge crew.

00:21:01.488 --> 00:21:03.979
I'm sure it was
very painful for him,

00:21:04.024 --> 00:21:05.389
but what you're saying is

00:21:05.425 --> 00:21:07.086
he's got a personal score
to settle.

00:21:07.127 --> 00:21:08.992
That's only part of it.

00:21:09.029 --> 00:21:11.793
I know Chakotay.

00:21:11.831 --> 00:21:14.925
This is his way
of taking responsibility.

00:21:14.968 --> 00:21:17.664
In his mind, he's trying
to protect the rest of us

00:21:17.704 --> 00:21:20.298
from a dangerous situation
which he created.

00:21:20.340 --> 00:21:21.807
Maybe, but that doesn't give him

00:21:21.841 --> 00:21:24.469
the privilege of ignoring
this ship's chain of command.

00:21:24.577 --> 00:21:25.475
I know that.

00:21:25.578 --> 00:21:27.239
It's just that...

00:21:27.280 --> 00:21:31.114
Chakotay would never tell you
any of this himself.

00:21:31.151 --> 00:21:33.949
And assuming we get him
back in one piece,

00:21:33.987 --> 00:21:34.954
you want to make sure

00:21:34.988 --> 00:21:36.922
I take his personal feelings
into account

00:21:36.956 --> 00:21:38.787
before I decide
how to discipline him.

00:21:40.393 --> 00:21:41.883
I know that you're
well within your rights

00:21:41.928 --> 00:21:43.896
to throw him into the brig,
but...

00:21:45.031 --> 00:21:47.363
Well...

00:21:47.400 --> 00:21:50.597
Chakotay is lucky to have
such a good friend.

00:21:51.738 --> 00:21:53.501
I'll tell you what.

00:21:55.375 --> 00:21:57.866
Why don't we deal
with getting him back

00:21:57.911 --> 00:21:59.173
in one piece first.

00:21:59.212 --> 00:22:02.340
We can worry about
the discipline later.

00:22:03.550 --> 00:22:04.574
Thank you.

00:22:10.090 --> 00:22:11.387
Computer, when will we enter

00:22:11.424 --> 00:22:13.051
the Kazon vessel's
scanner range?

00:22:13.093 --> 00:22:15.061
Approximately six minutes.

00:22:15.095 --> 00:22:17.222
Reduce power
to maneuvering thrusters

00:22:17.263 --> 00:22:19.197
and life support
to five percent.

00:22:19.232 --> 00:22:20.927
Cut all power to other systems.

00:22:29.509 --> 00:22:32.637
The Mostral should be here
in less than 20 hours.

00:22:32.679 --> 00:22:34.237
The Hobii in 15.

00:22:34.280 --> 00:22:36.111
Come look at this.

00:22:39.385 --> 00:22:42.252
Intermittent EM readings?

00:22:42.288 --> 00:22:44.347
I don't think so.

00:23:00.440 --> 00:23:03.136
Computer,
initiate continuous scans

00:23:03.176 --> 00:23:04.905
for the transporter oscillator.

00:23:04.944 --> 00:23:07.378
Initiating scans.

00:23:07.413 --> 00:23:09.381
Those aren't
normal fluctuations.

00:23:09.415 --> 00:23:12.009
They're energy spikes
from maneuvering thrusters.

00:23:12.051 --> 00:23:14.645
Probably a shuttle
running shadow maneuvers.

00:23:14.687 --> 00:23:16.450
He knows our scanners

00:23:16.523 --> 00:23:18.753
can't pinpoint
energy readings that low.

00:23:18.791 --> 00:23:20.088
Who?

00:23:20.126 --> 00:23:21.150
Maybe we can resonate

00:23:21.194 --> 00:23:23.025
a coherent polaron pulse
off his hull.

00:23:23.062 --> 00:23:24.996
Get a lock on him that way.

00:23:25.031 --> 00:23:27.022
Initiate a continuous
stream of pulses

00:23:27.066 --> 00:23:28.363
from the lateral deflectors.

00:23:28.401 --> 00:23:29.425
Maje?

00:23:34.207 --> 00:23:36.232
Come on, Seska.

00:23:36.276 --> 00:23:37.868
Where did you hide that module?

00:23:42.215 --> 00:23:43.409
There you are.

00:23:43.449 --> 00:23:44.643
Open a channel.

00:23:44.684 --> 00:23:46.481
To whom?

00:23:46.553 --> 00:23:49.113
Just transmit
on wide-band subspace.

00:23:49.155 --> 00:23:50.747
He'll hear me.

00:23:52.225 --> 00:23:54.420
Come on, find it!

00:23:54.460 --> 00:23:56.087
Hello, Chakotay.

00:23:56.129 --> 00:23:57.756
Very clever maneuvering,

00:23:57.797 --> 00:24:00.925
but I'm not about to let you
ruin all my hard work.

00:24:02.502 --> 00:24:04.129
Deploy a spread
of photonic charges

00:24:04.170 --> 00:24:07.071
centered on coordinates
124 by 217...

00:24:07.106 --> 00:24:09.438
20 percent nominal yield.

00:24:09.475 --> 00:24:11.102
That won't be enough.

00:24:11.144 --> 00:24:13.544
We want that shuttle intact.

00:24:17.684 --> 00:24:19.914
Got you.

00:24:19.953 --> 00:24:22.251
Computer, power
the antiproton generator.

00:24:22.288 --> 00:24:23.915
Generator ready.

00:24:23.957 --> 00:24:26.118
Target a concentrated beam
to these coordinates.

00:24:26.159 --> 00:24:27.285
Beam targeted.

00:24:28.995 --> 00:24:29.962
Initiate!

00:24:29.996 --> 00:24:31.793
The generator is off-line.

00:24:31.831 --> 00:24:33.560
Great.

00:24:33.600 --> 00:24:37.468
Computer, launch the automated
message beacon.

00:24:37.570 --> 00:24:39.037
Beacon launched.

00:24:39.072 --> 00:24:41.199
Now take the inertial dampers
off-line.

00:24:42.742 --> 00:24:44.471
He's lost control
of the shuttle.

00:24:44.510 --> 00:24:45.636
We have him.

00:24:45.678 --> 00:24:47.737
Lock the towing emitter
onto his vessel

00:24:47.780 --> 00:24:49.680
and bring him
into the main hangar.

00:25:02.228 --> 00:25:04.196
Culluh calling Seska.

00:25:04.230 --> 00:25:05.561
This is Seska.

00:25:05.598 --> 00:25:07.429
He's not here.

00:25:07.467 --> 00:25:09.264
He must have transported aboard.

00:25:09.302 --> 00:25:10.269
Find him!

00:25:10.303 --> 00:25:11.292
I'm right here.

00:25:14.941 --> 00:25:16.704
Activate the message beacon.

00:25:23.483 --> 00:25:25.974
Lovely to see you again.

00:25:39.498 --> 00:25:42.467
Captain, I'm detecting
a Federation beacon

00:25:42.501 --> 00:25:45.368
at bearing 059 mark 72.

00:25:45.404 --> 00:25:48.134
This one's definitely ours...
Starfleet issue.

00:25:48.174 --> 00:25:49.402
All stop.

00:25:49.442 --> 00:25:51.876
The beacon is transmitting
an automated message.

00:25:53.879 --> 00:25:55.471
It is from Commander Chakotay.

00:25:56.749 --> 00:25:58.046
On screen.

00:25:59.618 --> 00:26:00.846
...to Voyager.

00:26:00.886 --> 00:26:02.854
If this signal
has been activated,

00:26:02.888 --> 00:26:04.549
it means that I have destroyed

00:26:04.590 --> 00:26:06.717
the Nistrim's
transporter capabilities.

00:26:06.759 --> 00:26:10.354
Captain, I apologize for acting
without authorization,

00:26:10.396 --> 00:26:13.365
but I ask you
not to put the ship or crew

00:26:13.399 --> 00:26:15.799
in further jeopardy
by attempting to rescue me.

00:26:15.835 --> 00:26:18.429
It's unlikely
that I'm still alive.

00:26:18.471 --> 00:26:21.668
Chakotay to Voyager.

00:26:21.707 --> 00:26:23.174
If this signal
has been activated...

00:26:37.690 --> 00:26:39.749
You can go.

00:26:45.097 --> 00:26:47.930
I see the Nistrim
take orders from you now.

00:26:47.967 --> 00:26:51.403
Let's just say I'm in a position
of some influence,

00:26:51.437 --> 00:26:53.803
which is fortunate for you.

00:26:53.839 --> 00:26:56.672
Culluh wanted
to execute you immediately,

00:26:56.709 --> 00:27:00.042
but I convinced him that you'd
be a valuable prisoner

00:27:00.079 --> 00:27:03.378
and that I should be the one
to interrogate you.

00:27:03.415 --> 00:27:05.212
Lucky me.

00:27:05.251 --> 00:27:07.116
Would you like a drink?

00:27:07.152 --> 00:27:11.418
The Kazon word for this
is "enemy's blood."

00:27:11.457 --> 00:27:13.516
It's not exactly fine cognac,

00:27:13.559 --> 00:27:15.527
but I've developed
a taste for it.

00:27:15.561 --> 00:27:17.290
Try some.

00:27:19.532 --> 00:27:21.796
No, thanks.

00:27:23.168 --> 00:27:25.602
You know, I've got
to hand it to you.

00:27:25.638 --> 00:27:28.573
I thought all these months
answering to Janeway

00:27:28.607 --> 00:27:30.438
would have made you soft,

00:27:30.543 --> 00:27:33.034
but all you needed was
a little slap in the face

00:27:33.078 --> 00:27:36.445
to get that Maquis heart
of yours beating again.

00:27:36.515 --> 00:27:38.449
Here's to old times.

00:27:38.551 --> 00:27:40.917
I have no interest
in reminiscing with you.

00:27:40.953 --> 00:27:43.751
I destroyed
the transporter module.

00:27:43.789 --> 00:27:45.051
The game's over.

00:27:45.090 --> 00:27:48.116
What do I need with a single
transporter module

00:27:48.160 --> 00:27:50.651
when I've got your shuttle
and all its technology

00:27:50.696 --> 00:27:52.220
sitting in our hanger?

00:27:52.264 --> 00:27:54.994
I think you'll find
that technology useless.

00:27:55.034 --> 00:27:58.731
I wiped the computer core
before I transported.

00:28:00.773 --> 00:28:03.401
I should have anticipated that.

00:28:03.475 --> 00:28:06.376
So if you're going
to have me killed, just do it.

00:28:09.648 --> 00:28:11.980
You're still the noble one,
aren't you?

00:28:12.017 --> 00:28:14.110
Ready to die for your shipmates.

00:28:15.854 --> 00:28:17.287
You know, Chakotay,

00:28:17.323 --> 00:28:19.917
I may not have
the transporter anymore,

00:28:19.959 --> 00:28:22.587
but I've got something better.

00:28:22.628 --> 00:28:24.619
You.

00:28:24.663 --> 00:28:28.155
Maybe that's
all I really wanted.

00:28:28.200 --> 00:28:30.634
I've missed you.

00:28:30.669 --> 00:28:33.365
You can't possibly believe
that you and I could still...

00:28:33.405 --> 00:28:34.804
Don't flatter yourself.

00:28:34.840 --> 00:28:36.603
It was never that good.

00:28:36.642 --> 00:28:37.609
You might have been

00:28:37.643 --> 00:28:39.201
an interesting diversion
now and then,

00:28:39.244 --> 00:28:40.836
but I've always been
less interested in you

00:28:40.879 --> 00:28:43.245
than in the information
you could provide me with.

00:28:43.282 --> 00:28:45.375
First, you gave me
your Maquis secrets

00:28:45.417 --> 00:28:48.511
and now I want
Voyager's command codes.

00:28:49.989 --> 00:28:52.150
If you think I'm going
to give you those codes,

00:28:52.191 --> 00:28:55.285
you don't know me
as well as you think you do.

00:28:55.327 --> 00:28:59.195
Maybe not,
but for old time's sake,

00:28:59.231 --> 00:29:01.631
I'll let you in
on a little secret.

00:29:01.667 --> 00:29:03.726
There are half a dozen ships
from other Kazon sects

00:29:03.769 --> 00:29:05.930
on their way here right now.

00:29:05.971 --> 00:29:08.496
They're joining us
to help take Voyager.

00:29:08.540 --> 00:29:10.371
Why are you telling me this?

00:29:10.409 --> 00:29:14.004
I'm not a monster.

00:29:14.046 --> 00:29:17.277
I still care about Torres
and some of the others.

00:29:17.316 --> 00:29:19.113
I don't want to see
anybody get hurt.

00:29:19.151 --> 00:29:20.140
I never did.

00:29:20.185 --> 00:29:21.846
I'm touched.

00:29:21.887 --> 00:29:25.220
These Kazon aren't as
reasonable as you and I.

00:29:25.257 --> 00:29:27.054
I'm going to have to
use all my influence

00:29:27.092 --> 00:29:29.424
to make sure they
don't kill you all.

00:29:29.461 --> 00:29:31.759
But you've got to give me
something to work with.

00:29:31.797 --> 00:29:33.697
Voyager's not coming.

00:29:33.732 --> 00:29:35.256
I left them
explicit instructions

00:29:35.300 --> 00:29:36.289
not to follow me.

00:29:36.335 --> 00:29:39.304
So you can stop worrying
about people getting hurt.

00:29:42.474 --> 00:29:43.771
They'll come.

00:29:43.809 --> 00:29:45.868
They'd never leave
their First Officer

00:29:45.911 --> 00:29:47.378
in the hands of the Kazon.

00:29:47.413 --> 00:29:49.973
You may not give me
the command codes,

00:29:50.015 --> 00:29:55.578
but when Culluh gets through
with you, you'll wish you had.

00:30:00.426 --> 00:30:02.394
The message appears
to be authentic, Captain.

00:30:02.428 --> 00:30:04.020
We've got to go get him.

00:30:04.063 --> 00:30:05.792
Commander Chakotay has
expressly requested

00:30:05.831 --> 00:30:07.025
that we not attempt to do so.

00:30:07.066 --> 00:30:08.693
We don't have
to honor that request.

00:30:08.734 --> 00:30:10.065
Captain?

00:30:10.102 --> 00:30:12.627
If a rescue attempt forces
us to engage the Kazon,

00:30:12.671 --> 00:30:14.662
there is always a
possibility that more

00:30:14.707 --> 00:30:16.607
of our technology will
fall into their hands.

00:30:16.642 --> 00:30:17.904
Kim to the Captain.

00:30:17.943 --> 00:30:19.205
I'm picking up several vessels

00:30:19.244 --> 00:30:21.041
converging
on the Nistrim's location.

00:30:29.755 --> 00:30:31.450
My gut tells me

00:30:31.490 --> 00:30:33.720
we should go after Chakotay...

00:30:35.127 --> 00:30:39.291
but my better judgment,
tells me we should

00:30:39.331 --> 00:30:41.060
honor his request.

00:30:41.100 --> 00:30:46.003
I would never want you to ignore
your judgment, Captain,

00:30:46.038 --> 00:30:48.598
but let me ask you this.

00:30:48.640 --> 00:30:51.905
In your judgment,
how would the loss

00:30:51.944 --> 00:30:55.038
of our First Officer
affect this crew?

00:30:55.080 --> 00:30:58.243
What would it do
to the morale on this ship?

00:30:59.318 --> 00:31:00.876
Maybe this is an instance

00:31:00.919 --> 00:31:04.514
when your gut
is giving you better advice.

00:31:07.760 --> 00:31:09.159
Janeway to Conn.

00:31:09.194 --> 00:31:10.320
Paris here.

00:31:13.465 --> 00:31:15.126
Resume a course

00:31:15.167 --> 00:31:17.101
for Chakotay's shuttle.

00:31:17.136 --> 00:31:18.501
Aye, Captain.

00:31:24.243 --> 00:31:26.234
I'm losing patience, Federation.

00:31:33.318 --> 00:31:35.252
Just tell him
what he needs to know.

00:31:38.957 --> 00:31:41.425
She's quite a woman, isn't she?

00:31:42.895 --> 00:31:44.624
Does she rub your shoulders

00:31:44.663 --> 00:31:46.494
and tell you
you're the most exciting man

00:31:46.532 --> 00:31:48.329
she's ever known?

00:31:48.367 --> 00:31:49.800
That's what she
used to do for me.

00:31:51.670 --> 00:31:53.501
What's the matter?

00:31:53.539 --> 00:31:55.097
Didn't she tell you about us?

00:31:55.140 --> 00:31:59.509
Stop playing games
and give me the command codes.

00:31:59.545 --> 00:32:02.708
Flattery, devotion, sex...

00:32:02.748 --> 00:32:05.876
I always thought
she had a lot to offer a man.

00:32:05.918 --> 00:32:08.352
You talk too much, Federation,

00:32:08.387 --> 00:32:11.083
but you're not telling me
what I need to know.

00:32:11.123 --> 00:32:12.181
You're wrong, Culluh.

00:32:12.224 --> 00:32:14.419
I'm telling you exactly
what you need to know.

00:32:14.459 --> 00:32:16.723
She's using you.

00:32:16.762 --> 00:32:18.957
I'm the one who's using her.

00:32:18.997 --> 00:32:22.455
You've done an even better job
on him than you did on me.

00:32:22.501 --> 00:32:24.969
You talk to me, not to her.

00:32:25.003 --> 00:32:26.595
Then what's she doing here?

00:32:26.638 --> 00:32:28.333
Watching you work?!

00:32:28.373 --> 00:32:31.035
She used to like
to watch me work, too.

00:32:31.076 --> 00:32:33.135
I don't believe a word
you're saying,

00:32:33.178 --> 00:32:36.670
so you can stop trying
to distract me now

00:32:36.715 --> 00:32:38.683
and start answering questions.

00:32:38.717 --> 00:32:40.776
You know one thing
I especially liked?

00:32:40.819 --> 00:32:43.379
The little mole on her stomach.

00:32:45.791 --> 00:32:48.191
I guess you've seen it.

00:32:51.330 --> 00:32:53.924
I'm through
wasting my strength on you.

00:33:07.913 --> 00:33:12.350
Now give me the command codes.

00:33:13.485 --> 00:33:15.350
I'll give you something better.

00:33:15.387 --> 00:33:17.048
What?

00:33:17.089 --> 00:33:19.717
Firsthand information.

00:33:19.758 --> 00:33:21.589
Go ahead.

00:33:22.928 --> 00:33:25.692
When Seska's through with you...

00:33:28.600 --> 00:33:31.034
...she's going to kill you.

00:33:34.506 --> 00:33:35.996
He's delirious.

00:33:36.041 --> 00:33:38.271
He doesn't know
what he's saying.

00:33:38.310 --> 00:33:40.107
Give him some time.

00:33:41.813 --> 00:33:44.839
I'll be back in one hour.

00:33:44.883 --> 00:33:49.115
For his sake,
he'd better be more cooperative.

00:33:57.362 --> 00:34:00.422
Very clever ploy, Chakotay,

00:34:00.465 --> 00:34:03.525
but you know I'm not a killer.

00:34:12.911 --> 00:34:17.109
If I were, you'd have
been dead a long time ago.

00:34:28.192 --> 00:34:30.626
I have located the Nistrim
vessel on long-range sensors.

00:34:30.661 --> 00:34:32.720
Distance... .4 light-years.

00:34:32.763 --> 00:34:34.162
However, they are not alone.

00:34:34.198 --> 00:34:36.723
There are now at least
six other Kazon ships

00:34:36.767 --> 00:34:38.029
in the immediate vicinity.

00:34:38.068 --> 00:34:40.002
I didn't think Culluh
had that many ships.

00:34:40.037 --> 00:34:41.902
They must belong to enemy sects.

00:34:41.939 --> 00:34:43.429
That may be so,

00:34:43.473 --> 00:34:45.464
but the ships have not powered
their weapon systems.

00:34:45.509 --> 00:34:47.670
What do you make of it,
Neelix?

00:34:47.711 --> 00:34:49.736
It's certainly unusual
for rival Kazon

00:34:49.780 --> 00:34:50.838
sects to congregate peacefully.

00:34:50.881 --> 00:34:52.007
Is it possible

00:34:52.049 --> 00:34:54.347
the Nistrim have formed
an alliance with other sects?

00:34:55.619 --> 00:34:59.214
I've never known the Kazon to do
anything like that before.

00:34:59.256 --> 00:35:01.918
If the Nistrim have added
six ships to their force,

00:35:01.959 --> 00:35:04.985
it would be tactically unwise
to engage them.

00:35:05.028 --> 00:35:06.962
Then we'll just have
to find a way of getting

00:35:06.997 --> 00:35:09.022
Chakotay out of there
without picking a fight.

00:35:09.066 --> 00:35:11.057
We can transport him out.

00:35:11.101 --> 00:35:12.227
We would have to slow down

00:35:12.269 --> 00:35:14.863
once within transporter range,
giving the Kazon ample time

00:35:14.905 --> 00:35:15.929
to open fire.

00:35:15.973 --> 00:35:17.133
Not necessarily.

00:35:17.174 --> 00:35:19.438
We could beam him out
at warp speed

00:35:19.543 --> 00:35:21.306
without even slowing down.

00:35:21.345 --> 00:35:23.336
The Kazon would never
be able to catch us.

00:35:23.380 --> 00:35:25.678
That's difficult enough
when both ships

00:35:25.716 --> 00:35:26.910
are traveling at warp.

00:35:26.950 --> 00:35:28.281
The Kazon ship's
not even moving.

00:35:28.318 --> 00:35:29.785
I can compensate for that.

00:35:29.820 --> 00:35:30.787
How?

00:35:30.821 --> 00:35:32.345
By synchronizing
the transporter's

00:35:32.389 --> 00:35:34.789
annular confinement beam
to the warp core frequency.

00:35:34.825 --> 00:35:36.224
Maybe, but at a relative speed

00:35:36.260 --> 00:35:37.818
of two billion kilometers
per second,

00:35:37.861 --> 00:35:39.761
it's pretty tough
to get a lock on somebody.

00:35:39.796 --> 00:35:41.730
Ensign Kim is correct.

00:35:41.765 --> 00:35:42.732
We would risk scrambling

00:35:42.766 --> 00:35:44.427
his transporter signal
and killing him.

00:35:44.468 --> 00:35:47.266
It would be a direct violation
of Starfleet safety protocols.

00:35:47.304 --> 00:35:48.566
Do you have a better idea?

00:35:48.605 --> 00:35:50.470
Trust me, Captain.

00:35:50.540 --> 00:35:51.472
I can do it.

00:35:51.575 --> 00:35:53.202
How can you be so sure?

00:35:53.243 --> 00:35:55.473
Because I've done it before.

00:35:57.047 --> 00:35:58.571
When you are a Maquis,

00:35:58.615 --> 00:36:02.142
you don't always have the luxury
of following protocols.

00:36:05.122 --> 00:36:06.316
Ah!

00:36:06.356 --> 00:36:08.881
Jal Surat of the Mostral.

00:36:08.926 --> 00:36:12.521
May I present
Jal Loran of the Hobii

00:36:12.562 --> 00:36:15.895
and Jal Valek of the Oglamar?

00:36:15.933 --> 00:36:18.595
We've met before...

00:36:18.635 --> 00:36:20.933
in battle.

00:36:20.971 --> 00:36:25.601
Please, Jal Surat, sit down.

00:36:30.547 --> 00:36:35.314
Today is a day Kazon children
will remember for generations.

00:36:35.352 --> 00:36:38.810
Today is the day we put aside
our differences

00:36:38.855 --> 00:36:41.983
and join forces
to defeat Voyager.

00:36:43.627 --> 00:36:46.562
Today is the day
that marks the end

00:36:46.596 --> 00:36:49.326
of the supremacy
of the Relora and the Ogla

00:36:49.366 --> 00:36:54.827
because, after today, we will
have the Federation technology

00:36:54.871 --> 00:37:00.332
and the other sects
will run when they see us.

00:37:00.377 --> 00:37:04.313
That's a fine speech, Culluh,
but what makes you think

00:37:04.348 --> 00:37:08.341
Voyager won't use
this technology to defeat us?

00:37:08.385 --> 00:37:12.116
Because I have
Voyager's command codes.

00:37:12.155 --> 00:37:13.520
I have heard what you did

00:37:13.557 --> 00:37:16.788
to the Relora maje
and his companion...

00:37:16.827 --> 00:37:18.761
very impressive...

00:37:18.795 --> 00:37:23.926
but before I make an enemy of
these Federations, I want proof

00:37:23.967 --> 00:37:26.265
that you have
their command codes.

00:37:37.347 --> 00:37:40.180
May I present
Commander Chakotay...

00:37:40.217 --> 00:37:42.549
Voyager's First Officer.

00:37:55.065 --> 00:37:57.556
60 seconds to transporter range,
Captain.

00:37:57.601 --> 00:37:59.831
Bridge to Torres.
Have you located Chakotay?

00:37:59.870 --> 00:38:02.771
I'm reading Kazon life signs,
but still no Chakotay.

00:38:02.806 --> 00:38:04.205
Captain, I must remind you

00:38:04.241 --> 00:38:05.902
that we have
no direct evidence

00:38:05.942 --> 00:38:07.933
the Commander is still alive,
or if he is,

00:38:07.978 --> 00:38:09.172
that he's still
aboard that ship.

00:38:09.212 --> 00:38:10.372
I'm not conceding that yet.

00:38:10.414 --> 00:38:11.938
Can you give me anything,
B'Elanna?

00:38:13.216 --> 00:38:16.014
I'm picking up some kind
of localized dampening field.

00:38:16.053 --> 00:38:17.987
It's blocking
our targeting scanners.

00:38:18.021 --> 00:38:20.615
Maybe Seska's found a way
to hide Chakotay from us.

00:38:21.892 --> 00:38:23.325
You may be right.

00:38:23.360 --> 00:38:25.419
I've got to reinitialize
the targeting scanners

00:38:25.495 --> 00:38:28.191
to match the relative phase
of the dampening field.

00:38:30.767 --> 00:38:32.632
I've found him, Captain.

00:38:32.669 --> 00:38:34.102
He's still alive.

00:38:34.137 --> 00:38:35.900
Can you get him out of there?

00:38:35.939 --> 00:38:38.772
The damping field is disrupting
our transporter signal.

00:38:38.809 --> 00:38:40.174
I can't get a lock on him.

00:38:40.210 --> 00:38:41.438
Red Alert.

00:38:41.511 --> 00:38:43.376
Mr. Paris, take us out of warp.

00:38:46.583 --> 00:38:48.642
It's Voyager.

00:38:48.685 --> 00:38:49.777
Well, Culluh?

00:38:49.820 --> 00:38:51.378
What are you waiting for?

00:38:51.421 --> 00:38:53.719
Use the command codes
to disable them.

00:38:55.425 --> 00:38:57.757
Bridge,
this is First Maje Culluh.

00:38:57.794 --> 00:39:01.662
Lock weapons onto
the Federation ship and fire.

00:39:05.602 --> 00:39:07.627
Mr. Paris, evasive
pattern delta four.

00:39:07.671 --> 00:39:09.070
Mr. Tuvok, return fire.

00:39:09.106 --> 00:39:10.300
Firing phasers.

00:39:10.340 --> 00:39:11.307
Bridge to Torres.

00:39:11.341 --> 00:39:12.399
Can you transport Chakotay?

00:39:12.442 --> 00:39:14.410
I'm matching
the pattern buffer frequency

00:39:14.478 --> 00:39:15.945
to the Kazon dampening field.

00:39:15.979 --> 00:39:17.844
Make it fast.

00:39:17.881 --> 00:39:19.781
I've got a lock.

00:39:19.816 --> 00:39:21.716
Initiating transport.

00:39:36.466 --> 00:39:37.763
Do you have him, B'Elanna?

00:39:37.801 --> 00:39:38.790
I had him for a second,

00:39:38.835 --> 00:39:40.735
but they've remodulated
the dampening field.

00:39:40.770 --> 00:39:42.567
Can you compensate?

00:39:42.606 --> 00:39:44.733
I'm trying,
but I need more time.

00:39:44.774 --> 00:39:47.607
We'll try to hold them off,
but we don't have long.

00:39:47.644 --> 00:39:50.078
Mr. Tuvok, phasers to maximum.

00:39:50.113 --> 00:39:51.944
Let's give them
a little distraction.

00:39:55.352 --> 00:39:58.913
Why are you allowing them
to continue firing?

00:39:58.955 --> 00:40:00.650
It's taking longer
than I thought

00:40:00.690 --> 00:40:02.089
to interface with their systems.

00:40:02.125 --> 00:40:05.219
You must order your ships
to provide cover.

00:40:05.262 --> 00:40:08.857
I hope you know
what you're doing.

00:40:12.802 --> 00:40:14.326
The other Kazon vessels
have opened fire.

00:40:14.371 --> 00:40:16.999
Mr. Paris, evasive
pattern omega two.

00:40:17.040 --> 00:40:18.029
Aye, Captain.

00:40:18.074 --> 00:40:19.473
Bridge to Torres.

00:40:19.509 --> 00:40:21.340
You're going to have
to hurry it up down there.

00:40:21.378 --> 00:40:22.606
We can't hold them off
much longer.

00:40:22.646 --> 00:40:24.477
I'm doing the best I can.

00:40:24.581 --> 00:40:29.018
We're losing patience, Culluh.

00:40:32.522 --> 00:40:34.319
Where are you going?

00:40:34.357 --> 00:40:35.722
To the Bridge.

00:40:35.759 --> 00:40:36.817
I might have better luck

00:40:36.860 --> 00:40:38.828
interfacing with Voyager's
systems from there.

00:40:38.862 --> 00:40:40.489
I'll go with you.

00:40:40.564 --> 00:40:44.125
You'll stay right here.

00:40:45.268 --> 00:40:47.327
Aft shields down
to 23 percent, Captain.

00:40:47.370 --> 00:40:48.337
Bridge to Torres.

00:40:48.371 --> 00:40:50.168
Can you transport
Chakotay out or not?

00:40:50.207 --> 00:40:52.505
They've put the dampening field
on some kind

00:40:52.576 --> 00:40:54.305
of randomly fluctuating
modulation.

00:40:54.344 --> 00:40:57.006
It'll take me at least an hour
to match the phase variances.

00:40:57.047 --> 00:40:58.878
Shields at 16 percent.

00:40:58.915 --> 00:41:01.315
Captain, we must retreat.

00:41:01.351 --> 00:41:03.615
Lieutenant, just how localized
is that dampening field?

00:41:03.653 --> 00:41:05.018
A little more than two meters

00:41:05.055 --> 00:41:08.456
in diameter... just enough
to isolate Chakotay. Why?

00:41:08.558 --> 00:41:11.186
I think I've got an idea.

00:41:11.228 --> 00:41:14.254
I don't think you ever
had those command codes.

00:41:14.297 --> 00:41:15.730
I think you're a liar.

00:41:15.765 --> 00:41:17.562
What does it matter?

00:41:17.601 --> 00:41:18.829
If we work together,

00:41:18.868 --> 00:41:21.200
we don't need the command codes
to beat them.

00:41:21.238 --> 00:41:22.296
You're right.

00:41:22.339 --> 00:41:23.601
We can beat them,

00:41:23.640 --> 00:41:26.632
but we're going
to do it without you.

00:41:26.676 --> 00:41:29.509
We're taking your ship.

00:41:36.553 --> 00:41:38.748
Please stay where you are.

00:41:38.788 --> 00:41:41.313
You will find
that our transporters

00:41:41.358 --> 00:41:43.724
have rendered
your weapons useless.

00:41:45.929 --> 00:41:50.332
I will make you very sorry
for this, Culluh.

00:41:50.367 --> 00:41:51.925
Here are the terms, gentlemen.

00:41:51.968 --> 00:41:54.835
The safe return of our First
Officer and shuttlecraft

00:41:54.871 --> 00:41:56.771
in exchange for your freedom.

00:41:56.806 --> 00:42:00.537
I presume you will find that
an acceptable arrangement.

00:42:05.814 --> 00:42:09.875
Captain's Log, Stardate 49211.5.

00:42:09.918 --> 00:42:12.978
Now that Commander Chakotay
has made a full recovery,

00:42:13.022 --> 00:42:14.614
I'm faced
with the difficult task

00:42:14.657 --> 00:42:18.423
of responding to his failure
to follow procedure.

00:42:18.460 --> 00:42:19.893
Just tell me one thing.

00:42:19.928 --> 00:42:21.759
What were you thinking?

00:42:23.132 --> 00:42:26.465
About keeping our technology
out of Kazon hands.

00:42:26.568 --> 00:42:28.627
I thought if I did it on my own,

00:42:28.671 --> 00:42:30.866
I could keep the rest
of the crew out of danger.

00:42:30.906 --> 00:42:33.238
That may be
a very noble sentiment,

00:42:33.275 --> 00:42:36.802
but it wasn't
your decision to make.

00:42:41.283 --> 00:42:44.446
Oh, Chakotay...

00:42:44.486 --> 00:42:48.786
we've spent the last ten months
together on this ship.

00:42:48.824 --> 00:42:51.486
I thought we had
an understanding.

00:42:51.527 --> 00:42:54.223
Why did you choose
to ignore procedure?

00:42:56.365 --> 00:42:58.993
Seska was my problem...

00:42:59.034 --> 00:43:01.798
a problem I felt it
was my duty to solve.

00:43:01.837 --> 00:43:03.327
So you had a...

00:43:03.372 --> 00:43:05.806
personal score to settle.

00:43:07.643 --> 00:43:09.042
I thought I was doing
the right thing.

00:43:09.078 --> 00:43:10.443
Really?

00:43:10.479 --> 00:43:11.810
Tell me this.

00:43:17.286 --> 00:43:19.277
How do you expect me
to keep order

00:43:19.321 --> 00:43:21.084
when the First Officer
takes it upon himself

00:43:21.123 --> 00:43:23.284
to run off like some cowboy
because he decides

00:43:23.325 --> 00:43:25.919
it's a good idea?

00:43:25.961 --> 00:43:28.452
What you did was commendable.

00:43:28.497 --> 00:43:31.364
The way you did it was not.

00:43:31.400 --> 00:43:34.961
You set a terrible example,
and on a personal level,

00:43:35.003 --> 00:43:36.664
you've made my job
more difficult.

00:43:38.073 --> 00:43:42.009
If that's so, I regret it.

00:43:43.278 --> 00:43:45.337
I'm putting you on report,

00:43:45.380 --> 00:43:47.712
in case that means
anything anymore.

00:43:49.218 --> 00:43:51.778
It means something to me,
Captain.

00:43:51.820 --> 00:43:54.288
It means I've let you down

00:43:54.323 --> 00:43:56.257
and for that, I'm truly sorry.

00:43:56.291 --> 00:43:57.849
Bridge to ready room.

00:43:57.893 --> 00:43:59.485
Go ahead, Mr. Tuvok.

00:43:59.561 --> 00:44:01.028
I think you
and Commander Chakotay

00:44:01.063 --> 00:44:02.325
should come in here.

00:44:02.364 --> 00:44:04.093
On our way.

00:44:08.103 --> 00:44:10.936
I have located an automated
message beacon, Captain.

00:44:10.973 --> 00:44:12.167
Another one?

00:44:12.207 --> 00:44:14.141
It is a message
to Commander Chakotay

00:44:14.176 --> 00:44:15.541
from Seska.

00:44:15.577 --> 00:44:17.010
Would you like Mr. Kim

00:44:17.045 --> 00:44:19.206
to put it through
to your office?

00:44:19.248 --> 00:44:22.342
No, I think I've spent enough
time alone with Seska.

00:44:22.384 --> 00:44:23.851
Very well.

00:44:23.886 --> 00:44:25.251
Put it on screen.

00:44:25.788 --> 00:44:27.449
Hello, Chakotay.

00:44:27.523 --> 00:44:29.718
Congratulations on your victory.

00:44:29.758 --> 00:44:31.919
I look forward
to our next meeting.

00:44:31.960 --> 00:44:34.554
Oh, and there's something
you should know.

00:44:34.596 --> 00:44:35.893
While you were unconscious,

00:44:35.931 --> 00:44:38.627
I took the liberty of extracting
a sample of your DNA.

00:44:38.667 --> 00:44:41.363
I impregnated myself with it.

00:44:41.403 --> 00:44:45.897
So, I guess more congratulations
are in order.

00:44:45.941 --> 00:44:48.876
You're going to be a father.
